From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: accept empty strings in SetWindowTheme

Purpose: let a window opt out of visual styles with SetWindowTheme(hwnd,
L"", L""), as documented.
XP behavior: explorer turns theming off on the Start panel's log-off
toolbar this way and colours its labels with custom draw.
Wine before: AddAtomW rejected the empty string, so the call failed with
ERROR_INVALID_NAME without WM_THEMECHANGED; the toolbar kept its theme and
drew "log off" and "shut down" black instead of white.
Change: store a placeholder name that matches no theme class, so
OpenThemeData fails for that window; an empty sub-application name keeps
the default class.
Evidence: tests/window-theme-empty.c checks the HRESULT, WM_THEMECHANGED,
OpenThemeData and restoring the theme with NULL.
Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/uxtheme/nf-uxtheme-setwindowtheme
Scope: documented API behaviour, for every Wine application.
Old patches: 0043.
---
 dlls/uxtheme/system.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
index 8f96311..e959a23 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
@@ -591,7 +591,14 @@ static HRESULT UXTHEME_SetWindowProperty(HWND hwnd, ATOM aProp, LPCWSTR pszValue
     if(oldValue)
         DeleteAtom(oldValue);
     if(pszValue) {
-        ATOM atValue = AddAtomW(pszValue);
+        ATOM atValue;
+
+        /* AddAtomW rejects an empty string, but SetWindowTheme(hwnd, L"", L"")
+         * is the documented way to turn visual styles off for one window.
+         * Store a name that matches no theme class so OpenThemeData fails. */
+        if(!pszValue[0])
+            pszValue = L"0";
+        atValue = AddAtomW(pszValue);
         if(!atValue
            || !SetPropW(hwnd, (LPCWSTR)MAKEINTATOM(aProp), (LPWSTR)MAKEINTATOM(atValue))) {
             HRESULT hr = HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(GetLastError());
